  "source": {
    "authoredBasis": "New deterministic choice figure derived solely from the tool-prepared seed exercise 664, not an answer key or an original image. Evaluate the two source formulas C(x)=0.7^x and D(x)=0.4^x directly on a 0.01 x lattice and use the existing svgPath fallback for the sampled curves. Both formulas give y=1 at x=0. At x=-2, direct powers give C=100/49 and D=6.25; the shared canvas leaves both points visible. Axes, a unit grid, unlabeled landmark points, curve-continuation arrows, English C/D labels and solid/dashed distinction are authored instructional additions, not supplied source pixels. No false curve alternative or solution-set annotation is drawn. Bounding box [-2.8,7.75,3.3,-0.7] and unequal axis scaling are explicit; keepAspectRatio=false aligns the JSXGraph axes with the existing svgPath coordinate transform.",
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "alg8-c5-s2-n33",
        "exercise": "664",
        "text": "664。 简略地画出函数 $y=0.7^x$ 和 $y=0.4^x$ 的图象。 利用这两个图象解方程 $0.7^x=0.4^x$ 和不等式 $0.7^x>0.4^x$，$0.7^x<0.4^x$。"
      }
